{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>In the seventh month.</b> Sivan — and it is seventh to Kislev, in which the rains ceased." "<b>On the seventeenth day.</b> From here you learn that the Ark was submerged in the water eleven cubits. For it is written ״on the first day of the tenth month the tops of the mountains were seen״ — this is Av, which is tenth to Marcheshvan for the descent of the rains, and the waters were fifteen cubits above the mountains, and they diminished fifteen cubits from the first of Sivan to the first of Av in sixty days — that is one cubit per four days. It turns out that on the seventeenth of Sivan they had diminished only four cubits, and the Ark came to rest the next day. You have learned that it was submerged eleven cubits in the water above the tops of the mountains."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:56.707904398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}